/-!
# The event horizon of the Oppenheimer–Snyder collapse

Landau–Lifshitz, §102. The collapsing flat dust ball of `Collapse` (crunch at `τ_c`, boundary
radius `r_b(τ) = a(τ)χ_b`, `boundaryRadius`) inside the Schwarzschild field of mass `M`, with the
mass relation `9 M τ_c² = 2 χ_b³`, in one global chart: the Cartesian co-ordinates `(τ, x)` of
Painlevé and Gullstrand, `τ` the proper time of the freely falling observers.

* `osForm`: `ds² = −dτ² + ‖dx + β dτ‖²` with `β = V(τ, ‖x‖) x/‖x‖` and the speed `infallSpeed`
  `V = (2/3) r/(τ_c − τ)` in the ball, `√(2M/r)` outside; the two agree on the boundary
  (`dust_speed_boundary`), so the metric is continuous. `form_dust`, `form_lemaitre`: the spherical
  charts `sphChart` pull it back to `dustInterior` inside the ball and to the Lemaître chart
  `lemaitre` outside (`osForm_sphChart`). `spacetime`: before the crunch, and off the singularity
  `x = 0` after it.
* `IsFutureCausalCurve`: **the class of causal curves**: curves `τ ↦ (τ, x(τ))` parametrized by
  the time function, continuous, with a right derivative at every point (piecewise `C¹` curves are
  included) and a future causal velocity `(1, x′)` for the glued metric, `‖x′ + β‖ ≤ 1`
  (`isFutureCausal_iff`); they may cross the boundary of the ball. `causalPastScri`: the events from
  which such a curve reaches arbitrarily large radii (the causal past of future null infinity);
  `eventHorizon`: its boundary.
* `horizonRadius`: **the generator** `r_H(τ) = 3(r_b(τ) − (τ_c − τ))` up to
  `τ_H = τ_c − 4M/3`, `r_H = 2M` after: inside the ball the outgoing radial light ray
  `χ − η = const` (`dustRay`, `dustRay_null`) that crosses the boundary at `r = 2M` at `τ_H`
  (`boundaryRadius_horizonTime`), leaving the centre at `τ_c − 9M/2`; `horizon_generator`,
  `hasDerivWithinAt_horizonRadius`: it is an outgoing radial null curve, inside the ball before
  `τ_H` (`horizonRadius_le_boundaryRadius`) and the null sphere `r = 2M` after
  (`infallSpeed_two_mul`).
* **Non-escape** (`norm_le_horizonRadius_of_arc`, `norm_le_horizonRadius`,
  `notMem_causalPastScri`): the radius along a causal arc grows at most at the speed `1 − V` of the
  outgoing light rays (`eventually_slope_norm_lt`), `V` is one-sided Lipschitz above the generator
  (`infallSpeed_sub_le`), and Grönwall's inequality keeps an arc that starts below the generator
  below it, at `r ≤ 2M` (`horizonRadius_le`), across the boundary of the ball and up to the
  singularity. After `τ_H` the curves `x = 2M u` are such curves (`isFutureCausalCurve_horizon`).
* **Escape** (`mem_causalPastScri`): above the generator the outgoing ray of the dust leaves the
  ball before `τ_H` at a radius `> 2M` (`dustRay_exit`) and continues on a timelike radial curve to
  infinity (`exterior_escape`).
* **`causalPastScri_eq`**, **`eventHorizon_eq`**: the causal past of future null infinity is
  `‖x‖ > r_H(τ)`, and the event horizon is the hypersurface `‖x‖ = r_H(τ)` generated by the
  outgoing radial light rays through the crossing of the stellar surface with `r = 2M`.

The chart covers the whole Oppenheimer–Snyder spacetime outside the singularity (the regions I and
II of the Schwarzschild field outside the ball); the singularity `x = 0`, `τ ≥ τ_c`, is excluded.
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open Set Filter Topology
open scoped ContDiff Real InnerProductSpace

namespace ProjectAinos.GeneralRelativity.CollapseHorizon

open SmoothGeometry Collapse CollapseJunction

local notation "E3" => EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 3)

local notation "E" => MinkowskiModel 3

variable {M τc χb : ℝ}

/-! ### The spacetime of the collapse in the co-ordinates of Painlevé and Gullstrand -/

/-- The radial speed `V(τ, r)` of the freely falling observers: the dust `(2/3) r/(τ_c − τ)`
inside the ball, `r ≤ r_b(τ)`, `τ < τ_c`, and the speed `√(2M/r)` of fall from rest at
infinity outside. -/
def infallSpeed (M τc χb τ r : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  if τ < τc ∧ r ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ then 2 / 3 * r / (τc - τ) else Real.sqrt (2 * M / r)

/-- The rate `V/r`: `(2/3)/(τ_c − τ)` inside the ball, `√(2M/r)/r` outside. -/
def infallRate (M τc χb τ r : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  if τ < τc ∧ r ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ then 2 / 3 / (τc - τ) else Real.sqrt (2 * M / r) / r

/-- The shift vector `β = V(τ, ‖x‖) x/‖x‖` of the co-ordinates. -/
def shift (M τc χb τ : ℝ) (x : E3) : E3 := infallRate M τc χb τ ‖x‖ • x

/-- **The metric of the collapse** in the Cartesian co-ordinates `(τ, x) ∈ ℝ × ℝ³` of Painlevé
and Gullstrand: `ds² = −dτ² + ‖dx + β dτ‖²`, `β = V(τ, ‖x‖) x/‖x‖`. Inside the ball it is the
flat dust ball, outside the Schwarzschild field (`form_dust`, `form_lemaitre`); it is continuous
across the boundary `‖x‖ = r_b(τ)`, where the two speeds agree. -/
def osForm (M τc χb : ℝ) (p : ℝ × E3) (u u' : ℝ × E3) : ℝ :=
  -(u.1 * u'.1) + ⟪u.2 + u.1 • shift M τc χb p.1 p.2, u'.2 + u'.1 • shift M τc χb p.1 p.2⟫_ℝ

/-- The spacetime: before the crunch every point, after it every point off the centre (where the
singularity is). -/
def spacetime (τc : ℝ) : Set (ℝ × E3) := {p | p.1 < τc ∨ p.2 ≠ 0}

/-- A vector `u` at `p` is **future directed and causal**: `u^τ > 0` and `g(u, u) ≤ 0`. -/
def IsFutureCausal (M τc χb : ℝ) (p u : ℝ × E3) : Prop :=
  0 < u.1 ∧ osForm M τc χb p u u ≤ 0

/-- **A future-directed causal curve** from the time `τ₀`, parametrized by the time function `τ`
(every future causal curve with `dτ > 0` is such a curve after a change of parameter): a curve
`τ ↦ (τ, x(τ))` in the spacetime, continuous, with a right derivative `x′(τ)` at every point
(as a piecewise `C¹` curve has) and a future causal velocity `(1, x′(τ))`. It may cross the
boundary of the ball any number of times. -/
def IsFutureCausalCurve (M τc χb τ₀ : ℝ) (x : ℝ → E3) : Prop :=
  (∀ τ ∈ Ici τ₀, (τ, x τ) ∈ spacetime τc) ∧ ContinuousOn x (Ici τ₀) ∧
    ∀ τ ∈ Ici τ₀, ∃ v, HasDerivWithinAt x v (Ici τ) τ ∧ IsFutureCausal M τc χb (τ, x τ) (1, v)

/-- **The causal past of future null infinity**: the events from which a future-directed causal
curve reaches arbitrarily large radii. -/
def causalPastScri (M τc χb : ℝ) : Set (ℝ × E3) :=
  {p | p ∈ spacetime τc ∧ ∃ x : ℝ → E3, IsFutureCausalCurve M τc χb p.1 x ∧ x p.1 = p.2 ∧
    ∀ R : ℝ, ∃ τ ≥ p.1, R ≤ ‖x τ‖}

/-- **The event horizon**: the boundary of the causal past of future null infinity. -/
def eventHorizon (M τc χb : ℝ) : Set (ℝ × E3) := frontier (causalPastScri M τc χb)

/-- **The generator of the horizon**: `r_H(τ) = 3(r_b(τ) − (τ_c − τ))` until the boundary crosses
`r = 2M` at `τ_H = τ_c − 4M/3`, and `r_H = 2M` after. Inside the ball it is the outgoing radial
light ray `χ − η = const` through the event where the boundary crosses `r = 2M`; it leaves the
centre at `τ_c − 9M/2` (it is negative before). -/
def horizonRadius (M τc χb τ : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  if τ ≤ τc - 4 * M / 3 then 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) else 2 * M

theorem osForm_self (p : ℝ × E3) (v : E3) :
    osForm M τc χb p (1, v) (1, v) = -1 + ‖v + shift M τc χb p.1 p.2‖ ^ 2 := by
  simp [osForm]

/-- A velocity `(1, v)` is future causal exactly when `‖v + β‖ ≤ 1`. -/
theorem isFutureCausal_iff (p : ℝ × E3) (v : E3) :
    IsFutureCausal M τc χb p (1, v) ↔ ‖v + shift M τc χb p.1 p.2‖ ≤ 1 := by
  rw [IsFutureCausal, osForm_self]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨-, h⟩
    have h0 := norm_nonneg (v + shift M τc χb p.1 p.2)
    nlinarith
  · intro h
    refine ⟨one_pos, ?_⟩
    have h0 := norm_nonneg (v + shift M τc χb p.1 p.2)
    nlinarith


/-! ### The boundary of the ball and the generator -/

section Generator

variable (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb) (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3)

include hτc hmass in
/-- `r_b³ = (9M/2)(τ_c − τ)²`: the boundary falls from rest at infinity. -/
theorem boundaryRadius_cube {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc) :
    boundaryRadius τc χb τ ^ 3 = 9 / 2 * M * (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by
  rw [boundaryRadius, mul_pow, dustScale_cube hτc hτ]
  have h := hτc.ne'
  have hc : χb ^ 3 = 9 * M * τc ^ 2 / 2 := by linarith
  rw [div_pow, hc]
  field_simp

/-- Two nonnegative numbers compare as their cubes. -/
theorem le_iff_cube_le {a b : ℝ} (ha : 0 ≤ a) (hb : 0 ≤ b) : a ≤ b ↔ a ^ 3 ≤ b ^ 3 :=
  (pow_le_pow_iff_left₀ ha hb three_ne_zero).symm

theorem lt_iff_cube_lt {a b : ℝ} (ha : 0 ≤ a) (hb : 0 ≤ b) : a < b ↔ a ^ 3 < b ^ 3 :=
  (pow_lt_pow_iff_left₀ ha hb three_ne_zero).symm

include hM hτc hχ hmass

/-- On the boundary the speed of the dust is that of fall from rest at infinity:
`(2/3) r_b/(τ_c − τ) = √(2M/r_b)`. -/
theorem dust_speed_boundary {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc) :
    2 / 3 * boundaryRadius τc χb τ / (τc - τ) = Real.sqrt (2 * M / boundaryRadius τc χb τ) := by
  rw [sqrt_two_mul_div_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hτ, boundaryRate]
  ring

/-- The boundary is inside `r = 2M` exactly after `τ_H = τ_c − 4M/3`. -/
theorem boundaryRadius_le_iff {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc) :
    boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ 2 * M ↔ τc - 4 * M / 3 ≤ τ := by
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ
  have hs : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hτ
  rw [le_iff_cube_le hrb.le (by positivity), boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ]
  have h8 : (2 * M) ^ 3 = 9 / 2 * M * (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 := by ring
  rw [h8]
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hc
    have h1 : 4 * M / 3 < τc - τ := by linarith
    have h2 : (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 < (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by
      have : 0 < 4 * M / 3 := by positivity
      nlinarith
    have h3 : 9 / 2 * M * (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 < 9 / 2 * M * (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by
      have : 0 < 9 / 2 * M := by positivity
      nlinarith
    linarith
  · intro h
    have h1 : τc - τ ≤ 4 * M / 3 := by linarith
    have h2 : (τc - τ) ^ 2 ≤ (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 := by nlinarith
    have : 0 < 9 / 2 * M := by positivity
    nlinarith

theorem two_mul_lt_boundaryRadius {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc - 4 * M / 3) :
    2 * M < boundaryRadius τc χb τ := by
  have hτ' : τ < τc := by linarith
  by_contra h
  have := (boundaryRadius_le_iff hM hτc hχ hmass hτ').mp (not_lt.mp h)
  linarith

theorem boundaryRadius_horizonTime :
    boundaryRadius τc χb (τc - 4 * M / 3) = 2 * M := by
  have hτ : τc - 4 * M / 3 < τc := by linarith
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ
  refine (pow_left_inj₀ hrb.le (by positivity) three_ne_zero).mp ?_
  rw [boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ]
  ring

/-- Before `τ_H` the generator is inside the ball. -/
theorem horizonRadius_le_boundaryRadius {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ ≤ τc - 4 * M / 3) :
    3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ := by
  have hτ' : τ < τc := by linarith
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ'
  have hs : 4 * M / 3 ≤ τc - τ := by linarith
  have h3 : boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ 3 / 2 * (τc - τ) := by
    rw [le_iff_cube_le hrb.le (by linarith), boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ']
    nlinarith [sq_nonneg (τc - τ)]
  linarith

/-- The generator never exceeds `2M`. -/
theorem horizonRadius_le (τ : ℝ) : horizonRadius M τc χb τ ≤ 2 * M := by
  unfold horizonRadius
  split_ifs with hτ
  · have hτ' : τ < τc := by linarith
    have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ'
    have hs : 4 * M / 3 ≤ τc - τ := by linarith
    have h3 : boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ τc - τ + 2 * M / 3 := by
      rw [le_iff_cube_le hrb.le (by linarith), boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ']
      nlinarith [mul_nonneg (sq_nonneg (τc - τ - 4 * M / 3))
        (by linarith : (0 : ℝ) ≤ τc - τ + M / 6)]
    linarith
  · exact le_rfl

theorem horizonRadius_of_le {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τc - 4 * M / 3 ≤ τ) :
    horizonRadius M τc χb τ = 2 * M := by
  unfold horizonRadius
  split_ifs with h
  · have he : τ = τc - 4 * M / 3 := le_antisymm h hτ
    rw [he, boundaryRadius_horizonTime hM hτc hχ hmass]
    ring
  · rfl

end Generator


section Generator

variable (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb) (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3)
include hM hτc hχ hmass

/-- The speed at `r = 2M` after `τ_H` is the speed of light: the sphere `r = 2M` is a null
surface. -/
theorem infallSpeed_two_mul {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τc - 4 * M / 3 ≤ τ) :
    infallSpeed M τc χb τ (2 * M) = 1 := by
  unfold infallSpeed
  split_ifs with h
  · have hle := (boundaryRadius_le_iff hM hτc hχ hmass h.1).mpr hτ
    have heq : boundaryRadius τc χb τ = 2 * M := le_antisymm hle h.2
    have hs : τc - τ = 4 * M / 3 := by
      have hrb := boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass (χb := χb) h.1
      rw [heq] at hrb
      have hs0 : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr h.1
      have : (τc - τ) ^ 2 = (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 := by nlinarith
      have h43 : 0 < 4 * M / 3 := by positivity
      nlinarith [sq_nonneg (τc - τ - 4 * M / 3), sq_nonneg (τc - τ + 4 * M / 3)]
    rw [hs]
    field_simp
    ring
  · rw [div_self (by positivity), Real.sqrt_one]

/-- **The generator is an outgoing radial light ray**: its right derivative is `1 − V(τ, r_H)`,
the speed `dr/dτ = 1 − V` of the outgoing radial light rays of the metric. -/
theorem hasDerivWithinAt_horizonRadius (τ : ℝ) :
    HasDerivWithinAt (horizonRadius M τc χb)
      (1 - infallSpeed M τc χb τ (horizonRadius M τc χb τ)) (Ici τ) τ := by
  rcases lt_or_ge τ (τc - 4 * M / 3) with hτ | hτ
  · have hτ' : τ < τc := by linarith
    have hs : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hτ'
    have hev : horizonRadius M τc χb =ᶠ[𝓝 τ]
        fun t => 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb t - (τc - t)) := by
      filter_upwards [isOpen_Iio.mem_nhds hτ] with t ht
      simp [horizonRadius, show t ≤ τc - 4 * M / 3 from le_of_lt ht]
    have hd : HasDerivAt (fun t => 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb t - (τc - t)))
        (3 * (boundaryRate τc χb τ - (0 - 1))) τ :=
      ((hasDerivAt_boundaryRadius hτc hτ').sub ((hasDerivAt_const τ τc).sub
        (hasDerivAt_id τ))).const_mul 3
    have hval : horizonRadius M τc χb τ = 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) := by
      simp [horizonRadius, hτ.le]
    have hin := horizonRadius_le_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hτ.le
    refine (hd.congr_of_eventuallyEq hev).hasDerivWithinAt.congr_deriv ?_
    have hcond : τ < τc ∧ 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ :=
      ⟨hτ', hin⟩
    rw [hval, infallSpeed]
    simp only [hcond, and_self, ↓reduceIte, boundaryRate]
    field_simp
    ring
  · have hc : ∀ t ∈ Ici τ, horizonRadius M τc χb t = 2 * M := fun t ht =>
      horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass (le_trans hτ ht)
    rw [hc τ self_mem_Ici, infallSpeed_two_mul hM hτc hχ hmass hτ, sub_self]
    exact (hasDerivWithinAt_const τ (Ici τ) (2 * M)).congr (fun t ht => hc t ht)
      (hc τ self_mem_Ici)

end Generator


/-! ### Causal curves move outwards at most at the speed `1 − V` -/

/-- `V(τ, r) = (V/r) r`. -/
theorem infallRate_mul (τ r : ℝ) : infallRate M τc χb τ r * r = infallSpeed M τc χb τ r := by
  unfold infallRate infallSpeed
  split_ifs
  · ring
  · rcases eq_or_ne r 0 with h | h
    · simp [h]
    · field_simp

/-- `⟪x, β⟫ = V ‖x‖`. -/
theorem inner_shift (τ : ℝ) (x : E3) :
    ⟪x, shift M τc χb τ x⟫_ℝ = infallSpeed M τc χb τ ‖x‖ * ‖x‖ := by
  rw [shift, inner_smul_right, real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, ← infallRate_mul]
  ring

/-- The speed vanishes at the centre. -/
theorem infallSpeed_zero (τ : ℝ) : infallSpeed M τc χb τ 0 = 0 := by
  unfold infallSpeed
  split_ifs <;> simp

/-- **The radius along a future causal curve grows at most at the speed `1 − V`**: the upper
right Dini derivative of `‖x‖` is at most `1 − V(τ, ‖x(τ)‖)`. -/
theorem eventually_slope_norm_lt {x : ℝ → E3} {τ : ℝ} {v : E3}
    (hx : HasDerivWithinAt x v (Ici τ) τ) (hc : ‖v + shift M τc χb τ (x τ)‖ ≤ 1) {r₁ : ℝ}
    (hr : 1 - infallSpeed M τc χb τ ‖x τ‖ < r₁) :
    ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝[>] τ, (z - τ)⁻¹ * (‖x z‖ - ‖x τ‖) < r₁ := by
  have hset : Ici τ \ {τ} = Ioi τ := by
    ext z
    simp only [Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_Ici, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Set.mem_Ioi]
    exact ⟨fun h => lt_of_le_of_ne h.1 (Ne.symm h.2), fun h => ⟨h.le, h.ne'⟩⟩
  rcases eq_or_ne (x τ) 0 with h0 | h0
  · -- at the centre the slope tends to `‖v‖ ≤ 1`
    have hs := (hasDerivWithinAt_iff_tendsto_slope.mp hx)
    rw [hset] at hs
    have hn := (continuous_norm.tendsto v).comp hs
    have hv : ‖v‖ < r₁ := by
      have : shift M τc χb τ (x τ) = 0 := by simp [shift, h0]
      rw [this, add_zero] at hc
      rw [h0, norm_zero, infallSpeed_zero, sub_zero] at hr
      linarith
    filter_upwards [hn.eventually (gt_mem_nhds hv), self_mem_nhdsWithin] with z hz hz'
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, slope_def_module, h0, sub_zero] at hz
    rw [h0, norm_zero, sub_zero]
    rw [norm_smul, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_inv, abs_of_pos (sub_pos.mpr hz')] at hz
    exact hz
  · -- away from the centre `‖x‖` has the right derivative `⟪x, v⟫/‖x‖`
    have hpos : 0 < ‖x τ‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr h0
    have hsq := hx.norm_sq
    have hsqrt := hsq.sqrt (by positivity)
    have heq : (fun y => Real.sqrt (‖x y‖ ^ 2)) = fun y => ‖x y‖ := by
      funext y
      exact Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)
    rw [heq, Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)] at hsqrt
    have hs := hasDerivWithinAt_iff_tendsto_slope.mp hsqrt
    rw [hset] at hs
    have hD : 2 * ⟪x τ, v⟫_ℝ / (2 * ‖x τ‖) < r₁ := by
      have h1 : ⟪x τ, v + shift M τc χb τ (x τ)⟫_ℝ ≤ ‖x τ‖ :=
        (real_inner_le_norm _ _).trans (by nlinarith [norm_nonneg (x τ)])
      rw [inner_add_right, inner_shift] at h1
      rw [mul_div_mul_left _ _ two_ne_zero, div_lt_iff₀ hpos]
      nlinarith
    filter_upwards [hs.eventually (gt_mem_nhds hD)] with z hz
    simp only [slope_def_field] at hz
    rwa [div_eq_inv_mul] at hz


/-! ### Non-escape below the generator -/

/-- The speed `√(2M/r)` of fall from rest at infinity is Lipschitz with the constant `1/(4M)` on
`r ≥ 2M`. -/
theorem sqrt_sub_sqrt_le (hM : 0 < M) {a r : ℝ} (ha : 2 * M ≤ a) (har : a ≤ r) :
    Real.sqrt (2 * M / a) - Real.sqrt (2 * M / r) ≤ (r - a) / (4 * M) := by
  have hm := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr (show 0 < 2 * M by positivity)
  have ha0 : 0 < a := by linarith
  have hr0 : 0 < r := by linarith
  set m := Real.sqrt (2 * M) with hmdef
  set p := Real.sqrt a with hpdef
  set q := Real.sqrt r with hqdef
  have hp : 0 < p := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr ha0
  have hq : 0 < q := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr hr0
  have hm2 : m ^ 2 = 2 * M := Real.sq_sqrt (by positivity)
  have hp2 : p ^ 2 = a := Real.sq_sqrt ha0.le
  have hq2 : q ^ 2 = r := Real.sq_sqrt hr0.le
  have hmp : m ≤ p := Real.sqrt_le_sqrt ha
  have hpq : p ≤ q := Real.sqrt_le_sqrt har
  rw [Real.sqrt_div (by positivity), Real.sqrt_div (by positivity), ← hmdef, ← hpdef, ← hqdef,
    ← hp2, ← hq2]
  have h4M : 4 * M = 2 * m ^ 2 := by rw [hm2]; ring
  rw [h4M, div_sub_div _ _ hp.ne' hq.ne', div_le_div_iff₀ (by positivity) (by positivity)]
  have h1 : 0 ≤ q - p := by linarith
  have h2 : 2 * m ^ 3 ≤ p * q * (p + q) := by
    have hpq' : m * m ≤ p * q := mul_le_mul hmp (hmp.trans hpq) hm.le hp.le
    nlinarith [mul_le_mul hpq' (show m + m ≤ p + q by linarith) (by positivity) (by positivity)]
  nlinarith [mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left h2 h1]

section Trap

variable (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb) (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3)
include hM hτc hχ hmass

/-- **One-sided Lipschitz bound** above the generator:
`V(τ, r_H) − V(τ, r) ≤ (r − r_H)/(4M)` for `r ≥ r_H(τ)`. -/
theorem infallSpeed_sub_le {τ r : ℝ} (hr : horizonRadius M τc χb τ ≤ r) :
    infallSpeed M τc χb τ (horizonRadius M τc χb τ) - infallSpeed M τc χb τ r ≤
      (r - horizonRadius M τc χb τ) / (4 * M) := by
  rcases le_or_gt τ (τc - 4 * M / 3) with hτ | hτ
  · have hτ' : τ < τc := by linarith
    have hs : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hτ'
    have hin := horizonRadius_le_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hτ
    have hH : horizonRadius M τc χb τ = 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) := by
      simp [horizonRadius, hτ]
    rw [hH] at hr ⊢
    have hV : infallSpeed M τc χb τ (3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) =
        2 / 3 * (3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) / (τc - τ) := by
      simp [infallSpeed, hτ', hin]
    rw [hV]
    unfold infallSpeed
    split_ifs with hd
    · have : 2 / 3 * (3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) / (τc - τ) -
          2 / 3 * r / (τc - τ) ≤ 0 := by
        rw [← sub_div, div_nonpos_iff]
        right
        exact ⟨by linarith, hs.le⟩
      have : 0 ≤ (r - 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) / (4 * M) :=
        div_nonneg (by linarith) (by positivity)
      linarith
    · have hrb : boundaryRadius τc χb τ < r := by
        by_contra h
        exact hd ⟨hτ', not_lt.mp h⟩
      have hrb2 : 2 * M ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ := by
        rcases hτ.lt_or_eq with h | h
        · exact (two_mul_lt_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass h).le
        · rw [h, boundaryRadius_horizonTime hM hτc hχ hmass]
      have hV : 2 / 3 * (3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) / (τc - τ) ≤
          Real.sqrt (2 * M / boundaryRadius τc χb τ) := by
        rw [← dust_speed_boundary hM hτc hχ hmass hτ']
        exact div_le_div_of_nonneg_right (by linarith) hs.le
      have := sqrt_sub_sqrt_le hM hrb2 hrb.le
      have : (r - boundaryRadius τc χb τ) / (4 * M) ≤
          (r - 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ))) / (4 * M) :=
        div_le_div_of_nonneg_right (by linarith) (by positivity)
      linarith
  · have hH := horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass hτ.le
    rw [hH] at hr ⊢
    rw [infallSpeed_two_mul hM hτc hχ hmass hτ.le]
    unfold infallSpeed
    split_ifs with hd
    · have hle := (boundaryRadius_le_iff hM hτc hχ hmass hd.1).mpr hτ.le
      have hr2 : r = 2 * M := le_antisymm (hd.2.trans hle) hr
      exfalso
      have hb : boundaryRadius τc χb τ = 2 * M := le_antisymm hle (hr2 ▸ hd.2)
      have hrb := boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass (χb := χb) hd.1
      rw [hb] at hrb
      have hs0 : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hd.1
      have hs1 : τc - τ < 4 * M / 3 := by linarith
      have h1 : (τc - τ) ^ 2 < (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 := by nlinarith
      have h2 : 9 / 2 * M * (τc - τ) ^ 2 < 9 / 2 * M * (4 * M / 3) ^ 2 := by
        have : 0 < 9 / 2 * M := by positivity
        nlinarith
      nlinarith
    · have h := sqrt_sub_sqrt_le hM (le_refl (2 * M)) hr
      rwa [div_self (by positivity), Real.sqrt_one] at h


/-- The generator is continuous. -/
theorem continuous_horizonRadius : Continuous (horizonRadius M τc χb) := by
  have h : Continuous fun τ : ℝ =>
      if τ ≤ τc - 4 * M / 3 then 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τ - (τc - τ)) else 2 * M :=
    Continuous.if_le (continuous_const.mul ((continuous_boundaryRadius τc χb).sub
      (continuous_const.sub continuous_id))) continuous_const continuous_id
      continuous_const fun τ hτ => by
        rw [hτ, boundaryRadius_horizonTime hM hτc hχ hmass]
        ring
  exact h

/-- **No future causal arc crosses the generator outwards** (causal comparison): a future causal
arc on `[τ₀, τ]` (continuous, with a right derivative at every point of `[τ₀, τ)` that is a future
causal velocity), which starts on or below the generator, `‖x(τ₀)‖ ≤ r_H(τ₀)`, ends below it. The
difference `‖x‖ − r_H` has the upper right Dini derivative `≤ V(r_H) − V(‖x‖) ≤ (‖x‖ − r_H)/(4M)`
where it is nonnegative (`eventually_slope_norm_lt`, `hasDerivWithinAt_horizonRadius`,
`infallSpeed_sub_le`), and Grönwall's inequality keeps it nonpositive. The arc may end at the
singularity. -/
theorem norm_le_horizonRadius_of_arc {x : ℝ → E3} {τ₀ τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ₀ ≤ τ)
    (hc : ContinuousOn x (Icc τ₀ τ))
    (hd : ∀ t ∈ Ico τ₀ τ, ∃ v, HasDerivWithinAt x v (Ici t) t ∧
      IsFutureCausal M τc χb (t, x t) (1, v))
    (h0 : ‖x τ₀‖ ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb τ₀) : ‖x τ‖ ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb τ := by
  set K : ℝ := 1 / (4 * M) with hK
  set F : ℝ → ℝ := fun t => ‖x t‖ - horizonRadius M τc χb t with hF
  set f : ℝ → ℝ := fun t => max (F t) 0 with hf
  have hFc : ContinuousOn F (Icc τ₀ τ) :=
    (continuous_norm.comp_continuousOn hc).sub
      (continuous_horizonRadius hM hτc hχ hmass).continuousOn
  have hfc : ContinuousOn f (Icc τ₀ τ) := hFc.sup continuousOn_const
  have hgr := le_gronwallBound_of_liminf_deriv_right_le (f := f) (f' := fun t => K * f t)
    (δ := 0) (K := K) (ε := 0) hfc (fun t ht r hr => ?_) (by simp [hf, hF, h0])
    (fun t _ => by simp) τ ⟨hτ, le_rfl⟩
  · rw [gronwallBound_ε0_δ0] at hgr
    have : F τ ≤ 0 := le_trans (le_max_left _ _) hgr
    simp only [hF] at this
    linarith
  -- the right Dini derivative of `f`
  have ht0 : τ₀ ≤ t := ht.1
  obtain ⟨v, hv, hcv⟩ := hd t ht
  rw [isFutureCausal_iff] at hcv
  have hIoi : 𝓝[>] t ≤ 𝓝[Icc τ₀ τ] t := by
    rw [← nhdsWithin_Ioo_eq_nhdsGT ht.2]
    exact nhdsWithin_mono t fun z hz => ⟨le_trans ht0 (le_of_lt hz.1), le_of_lt hz.2⟩
  refine Eventually.frequently ?_
  by_cases hFt : F t < 0
  · have hev : ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝[>] t, F z < 0 :=
      hIoi ((hFc t (Ico_subset_Icc_self ht)).eventually (gt_mem_nhds hFt))
    have hft : f t = 0 := max_eq_right hFt.le
    have hr0 : 0 < r := by simpa [hft] using hr
    filter_upwards [hev] with z hz
    rw [show f z = 0 from max_eq_right hz.le, hft]
    simpa using hr0
  · have hFt' : 0 ≤ F t := not_lt.mp hFt
    have hft : f t = F t := max_eq_left hFt'
    set η := (r - K * F t) / 2 with hη
    have hηpos : 0 < η := by
      rw [hft] at hr
      linarith
    have hs1 := eventually_slope_norm_lt hv hcv
      (r₁ := 1 - infallSpeed M τc χb t ‖x t‖ + η) (by linarith)
    have hs2 : ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝[>] t, 1 - infallSpeed M τc χb t (horizonRadius M τc χb t) - η <
        (z - t)⁻¹ * (horizonRadius M τc χb z - horizonRadius M τc χb t) := by
      have h := hasDerivWithinAt_iff_tendsto_slope.mp
        (hasDerivWithinAt_horizonRadius hM hτc hχ hmass t)
      have hset : Ici t \ {t} = Ioi t := by
        ext z
        simp only [Set.mem_sdiff, Set.mem_Ici, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Set.mem_Ioi]
        exact ⟨fun h => lt_of_le_of_ne h.1 (Ne.symm h.2), fun h => ⟨h.le, h.ne'⟩⟩
      rw [hset] at h
      filter_upwards [h.eventually (lt_mem_nhds (by linarith : 1 - infallSpeed M τc χb t
        (horizonRadius M τc χb t) - η < 1 - infallSpeed M τc χb t (horizonRadius M τc χb t)))]
        with z hz
      simpa [slope_def_field, div_eq_inv_mul] using hz
    have hLip := infallSpeed_sub_le hM hτc hχ hmass (τ := t) (r := ‖x t‖)
      (by simp only [hF] at hFt'; linarith)
    filter_upwards [hs1, hs2, self_mem_nhdsWithin] with z hz1 hz2 hz
    have hzt : 0 < z - t := sub_pos.mpr hz
    have hslopeF : (z - t)⁻¹ * (F z - F t) < r := by
      have e : (z - t)⁻¹ * (F z - F t) = (z - t)⁻¹ * (‖x z‖ - ‖x t‖) -
          (z - t)⁻¹ * (horizonRadius M τc χb z - horizonRadius M τc χb t) := by
        simp only [hF]
        ring
      rw [e]
      have : (‖x t‖ - horizonRadius M τc χb t) / (4 * M) = K * F t := by
        simp only [hK, hF]
        ring
      linarith
    rw [hft]
    rcases le_or_gt 0 (F z) with hFz | hFz
    · rwa [show f z = F z from max_eq_left hFz]
    · rw [show f z = 0 from max_eq_right hFz.le]
      have : (z - t)⁻¹ * (0 - F t) ≤ 0 :=
        mul_nonpos_of_nonneg_of_nonpos (inv_nonneg.mpr hzt.le) (by linarith)
      have hr0 : 0 < r := by
        have : 0 ≤ K * F t := mul_nonneg (by positivity) hFt'
        linarith
      linarith

/-- **No future causal curve crosses the generator outwards** (`norm_le_horizonRadius_of_arc` on
every initial arc). -/
theorem norm_le_horizonRadius {x : ℝ → E3} {τ₀ : ℝ} (hx : IsFutureCausalCurve M τc χb τ₀ x)
    (h0 : ‖x τ₀‖ ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb τ₀) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ₀ ≤ τ) :
    ‖x τ‖ ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb τ :=
  norm_le_horizonRadius_of_arc hM hτc hχ hmass hτ (hx.2.1.mono Icc_subset_Ici_self)
    (fun t ht => hx.2.2 t ht.1) h0

/-- **Below the generator no event sees future null infinity**: from an event with
`‖x‖ ≤ r_H(τ)` every future causal curve stays in `r ≤ 2M`. -/
theorem notMem_causalPastScri {p : ℝ × E3} (hp : ‖p.2‖ ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb p.1) :
    p ∉ causalPastScri M τc χb := by
  rintro ⟨-, x, hx, hx0, hR⟩
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hle⟩ := hR (2 * M + 1)
  have h := norm_le_horizonRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hx (by rwa [hx0]) hτ
  have := horizonRadius_le hM hτc hχ hmass τ
  linarith

end Trap


/-! ### Escape above the generator -/

section Escape

/-- The shift along a direction: `β(τ, ρu) = V(τ, ρ) u` for a unit vector `u` and `ρ ≥ 0`. -/
theorem shift_smul {τ ρ : ℝ} (hρ : 0 ≤ ρ) {u : E3} (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) :
    shift M τc χb τ (ρ • u) = infallSpeed M τc χb τ ρ • u := by
  rw [shift, norm_smul, hu, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_nonneg hρ, smul_smul,
    infallRate_mul]

variable (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb) (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3)
include hM hτc hχ hmass

/-- The boundary radius decreases. -/
theorem boundaryRadius_anti {τ τ' : ℝ} (h : τ ≤ τ') (h' : τ' < τc) :
    boundaryRadius τc χb τ' ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ := by
  have hτ : τ < τc := lt_of_le_of_lt h h'
  rw [le_iff_cube_le (boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ h').le (boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ).le,
    boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass h', boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ]
  have h1 : 0 ≤ τc - τ' := by linarith
  have h2 : τc - τ' ≤ τc - τ := by linarith
  have : (τc - τ') ^ 2 ≤ (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by nlinarith
  have : 0 < 9 / 2 * M := by positivity
  nlinarith

/-- Outside the ball, or on its boundary, the speed is `√(2M/r)`. -/
theorem infallSpeed_eq_sqrt {τ r : ℝ} (h : τc ≤ τ ∨ boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ r) :
    infallSpeed M τc χb τ r = Real.sqrt (2 * M / r) := by
  unfold infallSpeed
  split_ifs with hd
  · rcases h with h | h
    · exact absurd hd.1 (not_lt.mpr h)
    · rw [le_antisymm hd.2 h]
      exact dust_speed_boundary hM hτc hχ hmass hd.1
  · rfl

/-- **The escaping curves of the exterior**: from an event at the radius `R₁ > 2M` outside the
ball (or on its boundary), the radial curve `r = R₁ + δ(τ − τ₁)` with `δ = (1 − √(2M/R₁))/2` is
future timelike, stays outside the ball and reaches arbitrarily large radii. -/
theorem exterior_escape {τ₁ R₁ : ℝ} {u : E3} (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) (hR : 2 * M < R₁)
    (hext : τ₁ < τc → boundaryRadius τc χb τ₁ ≤ R₁) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ₁ ≤ τ) :
    let δ := (1 - Real.sqrt (2 * M / R₁)) / 2
    (τ, (R₁ + δ * (τ - τ₁)) • u) ∈ spacetime τc ∧
      HasDerivAt (fun t => (R₁ + δ * (t - τ₁)) • u) (δ • u) τ ∧
      ‖δ • u + shift M τc χb τ ((R₁ + δ * (τ - τ₁)) • u)‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      ‖(R₁ + δ * (τ - τ₁)) • u‖ = R₁ + δ * (τ - τ₁) := by
  intro δ
  have hR0 : 0 < R₁ := by linarith
  have hsq : Real.sqrt (2 * M / R₁) < 1 := by
    rw [Real.sqrt_lt' one_pos, one_pow, div_lt_one hR0]
    exact hR
  have hδ : 0 < δ := by
    simp only [δ]
    linarith
  set ρ := R₁ + δ * (τ - τ₁) with hρ
  have hρR : R₁ ≤ ρ := by nlinarith
  have hρ0 : 0 < ρ := by linarith
  have hnorm : ‖ρ • u‖ = ρ := by rw [norm_smul, hu, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_pos hρ0]
  refine ⟨Or.inr ?_, ?_, ?_, hnorm⟩
  · rw [← norm_pos_iff, hnorm]
    exact hρ0
  · have h := ((((hasDerivAt_id τ).sub_const τ₁).const_mul δ).const_add R₁).smul_const u
    simpa using h
  · have hext' : τc ≤ τ ∨ boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ ρ := by
      rcases le_or_gt τc τ with h | h
      · exact Or.inl h
      · right
        have h1 : τ₁ < τc := lt_of_le_of_lt hτ h
        exact (boundaryRadius_anti hM hτc hχ hmass hτ h).trans ((hext h1).trans hρR)
    rw [shift_smul hρ0.le hu, infallSpeed_eq_sqrt hM hτc hχ hmass hext', ← add_smul, norm_smul,
      hu, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs]
    have hs0 := Real.sqrt_nonneg (2 * M / ρ)
    have hs1 : Real.sqrt (2 * M / ρ) ≤ Real.sqrt (2 * M / R₁) :=
      Real.sqrt_le_sqrt (div_le_div_of_nonneg_left (by positivity) hR0 hρR)
    rw [abs_of_nonneg (by positivity)]
    simp only [δ] at hδ ⊢
    linarith


omit hM in
/-- The comparison of `c r_b(τ)` with `3(τ_c − τ)` is the comparison of `c³M/6` with
`τ_c − τ`. -/
theorem mul_boundaryRadius_le_iff {c τ : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) (hτ : τ < τc) :
    c * boundaryRadius τc χb τ ≤ 3 * (τc - τ) ↔ c ^ 3 * M / 6 ≤ τc - τ := by
  have hs : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hτ
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ
  rw [le_iff_cube_le (by positivity) (by positivity), mul_pow,
    boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h2 : 0 < (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith
  · intro h
    have h2 : 0 < (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith

omit hM in
theorem le_mul_boundaryRadius_iff {c τ : ℝ} (hc : 0 ≤ c) (hτ : τ < τc) :
    3 * (τc - τ) ≤ c * boundaryRadius τc χb τ ↔ τc - τ ≤ c ^ 3 * M / 6 := by
  have hs : 0 < τc - τ := sub_pos.mpr hτ
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ
  rw [le_iff_cube_le (by positivity) (by positivity), mul_pow c,
    boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h2 : 0 < (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith
  · intro h
    have h2 : 0 < (τc - τ) ^ 2 := by positivity
    nlinarith

/-- **The outgoing radial light rays in the dust**: `r(τ) = λ r_b(τ) − 3(τ_c − τ)`, the rays
`χ − η = const` of the comoving conformal co-ordinates; `λ = 3` is the generator. -/
def dustRay (τc χb lam τ : ℝ) : ℝ := lam * boundaryRadius τc χb τ - 3 * (τc - τ)

omit hM hχ hmass in
theorem hasDerivAt_dustRay (lam : ℝ) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc) :
    HasDerivAt (dustRay τc χb lam) (lam * boundaryRate τc χb τ + 3) τ := by
  have h1 : HasDerivAt (fun t => lam * boundaryRadius τc χb t) (lam * boundaryRate τc χb τ) τ :=
    (hasDerivAt_boundaryRadius hτc hτ).const_mul lam
  have h2 : HasDerivAt (fun t : ℝ => 3 * (τc - t)) (3 * (0 - 1)) τ :=
    ((hasDerivAt_const τ τc).sub (hasDerivAt_id τ)).const_mul 3
  exact (h1.fun_sub h2).congr_deriv (by ring)

omit hM hτc hχ hmass in
/-- The rays are null: `dr/dτ + V = 1` with the dust speed `V = (2/3) r/(τ_c − τ)`. -/
theorem dustRay_null (lam : ℝ) {τ : ℝ} (hτ : τ < τc) :
    lam * boundaryRate τc χb τ + 3 + 2 / 3 * dustRay τc χb lam τ / (τc - τ) = 1 := by
  have hs : τc - τ ≠ 0 := (sub_pos.mpr hτ).ne'
  simp only [boundaryRate, dustRay]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- **The dust part of an escaping curve.** Let `p` be an event of the ball above the generator
before `τ_H`, at the radius `ρ_p`. The outgoing ray through it, with `λ = (ρ_p + 3(τ_c − τ_p))/r_b`,
stays in the ball, at a nonnegative radius, until it leaves it at
`τ_e = τ_c − (λ − 1)³M/6 < τ_H`, on the boundary at the radius `r_b(τ_e) > 2M`. -/
theorem dustRay_exit {τp ρp : ℝ} (hτp : τp < τc - 4 * M / 3) (hρ0 : 0 ≤ ρp)
    (hρb : ρp ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τp)
    (hρH : 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τp - (τc - τp)) < ρp) :
    let lam := (ρp + 3 * (τc - τp)) / boundaryRadius τc χb τp
    let τe := τc - (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6
    dustRay τc χb lam τp = ρp ∧ 3 < lam ∧ τp ≤ τe ∧ τe < τc - 4 * M / 3 ∧
      dustRay τc χb lam τe = boundaryRadius τc χb τe ∧ 2 * M < boundaryRadius τc χb τe ∧
      ∀ τ, τp ≤ τ → τ ≤ τe →
        0 ≤ dustRay τc χb lam τ ∧ dustRay τc χb lam τ ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τ := by
  intro lam τe
  have hτp' : τp < τc := by linarith
  have hsp : 0 < τc - τp := sub_pos.mpr hτp'
  have hrb := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτp'
  have hlam : lam * boundaryRadius τc χb τp = ρp + 3 * (τc - τp) := by
    simp only [lam]
    field_simp
  have hray : dustRay τc χb lam τp = ρp := by
    simp only [dustRay]
    linarith
  have h3 : 3 < lam := by
    by_contra h
    have : lam * boundaryRadius τc χb τp ≤ 3 * boundaryRadius τc χb τp :=
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right (not_lt.mp h) hrb.le
    linarith
  have hl1 : 0 ≤ lam - 1 := by linarith
  -- the exit time
  have hse : (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6 ≤ τc - τp :=
    (mul_boundaryRadius_le_iff hτc hχ hmass hl1 hτp').mp (by nlinarith)
  have hseH : 4 * M / 3 < (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6 := by
    have h2 : (2 : ℝ) ^ 3 < (lam - 1) ^ 3 := by
      apply pow_lt_pow_left₀ (by linarith) (by norm_num) (by norm_num)
    nlinarith
  have hτe : τe < τc - 4 * M / 3 := by
    simp only [τe]
    linarith
  have hτe' : τe < τc := by linarith
  have hpe : τp ≤ τe := by
    simp only [τe]
    linarith
  have hsτe : τc - τe = (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6 := by
    simp only [τe]
    ring
  -- the ray on the boundary at the exit
  have hexit : dustRay τc χb lam τe = boundaryRadius τc χb τe := by
    have hle := (mul_boundaryRadius_le_iff hτc hχ hmass hl1 hτe').mpr hsτe.ge
    have hge : 3 * (τc - τe) ≤ (lam - 1) * boundaryRadius τc χb τe := by
      by_contra hc
      push Not at hc
      have hrbe := boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτe'
      have hc3 : ((lam - 1) * boundaryRadius τc χb τe) ^ 3 < (3 * (τc - τe)) ^ 3 :=
        pow_lt_pow_left₀ hc (by positivity) (by norm_num)
      rw [mul_pow, boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτe', hsτe] at hc3
      have : 0 < (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6 := by
        have : 0 < (lam - 1) ^ 3 := pow_pos (by linarith) 3
        positivity
      nlinarith
    simp only [dustRay]
    linarith
  have hrbe : 2 * M < boundaryRadius τc χb τe := two_mul_lt_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hτe
  refine ⟨hray, h3, hpe, hτe, hexit, hrbe, fun τ hτ1 hτ2 => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · -- the radius stays nonnegative
    have hτ' : τ < τc := lt_of_le_of_lt hτ2 hτe'
    have hlam0 : 0 ≤ lam := by linarith
    have hpp : τc - τp ≤ lam ^ 3 * M / 6 :=
      (le_mul_boundaryRadius_iff hτc hχ hmass hlam0 hτp').mp (by linarith)
    have := (le_mul_boundaryRadius_iff hτc hχ hmass hlam0 hτ').mpr (by linarith)
    simp only [dustRay]
    linarith
  · have hτ' : τ < τc := lt_of_le_of_lt hτ2 hτe'
    have := (mul_boundaryRadius_le_iff hτc hχ hmass hl1 hτ').mpr (by linarith)
    simp only [dustRay]
    linarith


/-- A unit vector along `x`, or a fixed one at the centre. -/
def direction (x : E3) : E3 := if x = 0 then EuclideanSpace.single 0 1 else ‖x‖⁻¹ • x

omit hM hτc hχ hmass in
theorem norm_direction (x : E3) : ‖direction x‖ = 1 := by
  unfold direction
  split_ifs with h
  · simp
  · rw [norm_smul, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_inv, abs_norm, inv_mul_cancel₀ (norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr h)]

omit hM hτc hχ hmass in
theorem norm_smul_direction (x : E3) : ‖x‖ • direction x = x := by
  unfold direction
  split_ifs with h
  · simp [h]
  · rw [smul_smul, mul_inv_cancel₀ (norm_ne_zero_iff.mpr h), one_smul]

/-- **Escape above the generator**: from every event of the spacetime strictly above the
generator, `‖x‖ > r_H(τ)`, an explicit future causal curve reaches arbitrarily large radii. From the
ball it follows the outgoing radial light ray in the dust (`dustRay`) out of the ball, which it
leaves before `τ_H` at a radius `> 2M` (`dustRay_exit`), and continues by the timelike radial
curve `exterior_escape`; from outside the ball it is that curve. -/
theorem mem_causalPastScri {p : ℝ × E3} (hp : p ∈ spacetime τc)
    (h : horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 < ‖p.2‖) : p ∈ causalPastScri M τc χb := by
  obtain ⟨τp, xp⟩ := p
  simp only at h hp
  refine ⟨hp, ?_⟩
  set u := direction xp with hudef
  have hu : ‖u‖ = 1 := norm_direction xp
  have hxu : ‖xp‖ • u = xp := norm_smul_direction xp
  by_cases hd : τp < τc ∧ ‖xp‖ ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb τp
  · -- the event is in the ball, before `τ_H`
    have hτH : τp < τc - 4 * M / 3 := by
      by_contra hc
      have hc' : τc - 4 * M / 3 ≤ τp := not_lt.mp hc
      rw [horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass hc'] at h
      have := (boundaryRadius_le_iff hM hτc hχ hmass hd.1).mpr hc'
      linarith [hd.2]
    have hH : horizonRadius M τc χb τp = 3 * (boundaryRadius τc χb τp - (τc - τp)) := by
      simp [horizonRadius, hτH.le]
    rw [hH] at h
    obtain ⟨hray, h3, hpe, hτe, hexit, hrbe, hin⟩ :=
      dustRay_exit hM hτc hχ hmass hτH (norm_nonneg xp) hd.2 h
    set lam := (‖xp‖ + 3 * (τc - τp)) / boundaryRadius τc χb τp with hlam
    set τe := τc - (lam - 1) ^ 3 * M / 6 with hτedef
    set R₁ := boundaryRadius τc χb τe with hR₁
    set δ := (1 - Real.sqrt (2 * M / R₁)) / 2 with hδ
    have hτe' : τe < τc := by linarith
    set y : ℝ → E3 := fun τ =>
      if τ ≤ τe then dustRay τc χb lam τ • u else (R₁ + δ * (τ - τe)) • u with hy
    have hyτe : ∀ τ, τe ≤ τ → y τ = (R₁ + δ * (τ - τe)) • u := by
      intro τ hτ
      simp only [hy]
      split_ifs with h'
      · have : τ = τe := le_antisymm h' hτ
        rw [this, hexit, sub_self, mul_zero, add_zero]
      · rfl
    have hesc (τ : ℝ) (hτ : τe ≤ τ) := exterior_escape hM hτc hχ hmass hu hrbe
      (fun _ => le_rfl) hτ
    have hR0 : 0 < R₁ := by linarith
    have hδ0 : 0 < δ := by
      have : Real.sqrt (2 * M / R₁) < 1 := by
        rw [Real.sqrt_lt' one_pos, one_pow, div_lt_one hR0]
        exact hrbe
      simp only [hδ]
      linarith
    refine ⟨y, ⟨fun τ hτ => ?_, ?_, fun τ hτ => ?_⟩, ?_, fun R => ?_⟩
    · -- in the spacetime
      rcases le_or_gt τ τe with h' | h'
      · exact Or.inl (lt_of_le_of_lt h' hτe')
      · rw [hyτe τ h'.le]
        exact (hesc τ h'.le).1
    · -- continuity
      refine Continuous.continuousOn ?_
      refine Continuous.if_le (((continuous_const.mul (continuous_boundaryRadius τc χb)).sub
        (continuous_const.mul (continuous_const.sub continuous_id))).smul continuous_const)
        ((continuous_const.add (continuous_const.mul (continuous_id.sub continuous_const))).smul
          continuous_const) continuous_id continuous_const fun τ hτ => ?_
      rw [hτ, hexit, sub_self, mul_zero, add_zero]
    · -- the velocity
      rcases lt_or_ge τ τe with h' | h'
      · have hτ' : τ < τc := lt_of_lt_of_le h' hτe'.le
        have hev : y =ᶠ[𝓝 τ] fun t => dustRay τc χb lam t • u := by
          filter_upwards [isOpen_Iio.mem_nhds h'] with t ht
          simp [hy, show t ≤ τe from le_of_lt ht]
        have hD := ((hasDerivAt_dustRay hτc lam hτ').smul_const u).congr_of_eventuallyEq hev
        refine ⟨_, hD.hasDerivWithinAt, ?_⟩
        rw [isFutureCausal_iff]
        have hyτ : y τ = dustRay τc χb lam τ • u := by simp [hy, h'.le]
        obtain ⟨hr0, hrb⟩ := hin τ hτ h'.le
        simp only
        rw [hyτ, shift_smul hr0 hu, ← add_smul, norm_smul, hu, mul_one]
        have hV : infallSpeed M τc χb τ (dustRay τc χb lam τ) =
            2 / 3 * dustRay τc χb lam τ / (τc - τ) := by
          simp [infallSpeed, hτ', hrb]
        rw [hV, dustRay_null lam hτ']
        simp
      · obtain ⟨-, hD, hc, -⟩ := hesc τ h'
        refine ⟨δ • u, (hD.hasDerivWithinAt.congr (fun t ht => hyτe t (le_trans h' ht))
          (hyτe τ h')), ?_⟩
        rw [isFutureCausal_iff]
        simp only
        rw [hyτe τ h']
        exact hc
    · -- the initial point
      simp only [hy, hpe, ↓reduceIte, hray, hxu]
    · -- arbitrarily large radii
      refine ⟨τe + (|R| + 1) / δ, by
        have : 0 ≤ (|R| + 1) / δ := by positivity
        linarith, ?_⟩
      have hτ : τe ≤ τe + (|R| + 1) / δ := by
        have : 0 ≤ (|R| + 1) / δ := by positivity
        linarith
      rw [hyτe _ hτ, (hesc _ hτ).2.2.2]
      have : δ * (τe + (|R| + 1) / δ - τe) = |R| + 1 := by
        field_simp
        ring
      rw [this]
      linarith [le_abs_self R]
  · -- the event is outside the ball, outside `r = 2M`
    have hR : 2 * M < ‖xp‖ := by
      rcases le_or_gt (τc - 4 * M / 3) τp with hτ | hτ
      · rwa [horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass hτ] at h
      · have hτ' : τp < τc := by linarith
        have := two_mul_lt_boundaryRadius hM hτc hχ hmass hτ
        have : boundaryRadius τc χb τp < ‖xp‖ := by
          by_contra hc
          exact hd ⟨hτ', not_lt.mp hc⟩
        linarith
    have hext : τp < τc → boundaryRadius τc χb τp ≤ ‖xp‖ := fun hτ => by
      by_contra hc
      exact hd ⟨hτ, (not_le.mp hc).le⟩
    set δ := (1 - Real.sqrt (2 * M / ‖xp‖)) / 2 with hδ
    have hR0 : 0 < ‖xp‖ := by linarith
    have hδ0 : 0 < δ := by
      have : Real.sqrt (2 * M / ‖xp‖) < 1 := by
        rw [Real.sqrt_lt' one_pos, one_pow, div_lt_one hR0]
        exact hR
      simp only [hδ]
      linarith
    have hesc (τ : ℝ) (hτ : τp ≤ τ) := exterior_escape hM hτc hχ hmass hu hR hext hτ
    refine ⟨fun τ => (‖xp‖ + δ * (τ - τp)) • u, ⟨fun τ hτ => (hesc τ hτ).1, ?_,
      fun τ hτ => ⟨δ • u, (hesc τ hτ).2.1.hasDerivWithinAt, ?_⟩⟩, ?_, fun R => ?_⟩
    · exact Continuous.continuousOn ((continuous_const.add (continuous_const.mul
        (continuous_id.sub continuous_const))).smul continuous_const)
    · rw [isFutureCausal_iff]
      exact (hesc τ hτ).2.2.1
    · simp only [sub_self, mul_zero, add_zero, hxu]
    · refine ⟨τp + (|R| + 1) / δ, by
        have : 0 ≤ (|R| + 1) / δ := by positivity
        linarith, ?_⟩
      have hτ : τp ≤ τp + (|R| + 1) / δ := by
        have : 0 ≤ (|R| + 1) / δ := by positivity
        linarith
      rw [(hesc _ hτ).2.2.2]
      have : δ * (τp + (|R| + 1) / δ - τp) = |R| + 1 := by
        field_simp
        ring
      rw [this]
      linarith [le_abs_self R]

end Escape


/-! ### The event horizon -/

section Horizon

variable (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb) (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3)
include hM hτc hχ hmass

/-- **The causal past of future null infinity is the region above the generator**:
an event sees future null infinity exactly when `‖x‖ > r_H(τ)`. -/
theorem causalPastScri_eq :
    causalPastScri M τc χb = {p : ℝ × E3 | horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 < ‖p.2‖} := by
  ext p
  constructor
  · intro hp
    by_contra hc
    exact notMem_causalPastScri hM hτc hχ hmass (not_lt.mp hc) hp
  · intro hp
    refine mem_causalPastScri hM hτc hχ hmass ?_ hp
    rcases lt_or_ge p.1 τc with h | h
    · exact Or.inl h
    · right
      have : τc - 4 * M / 3 ≤ p.1 := by linarith
      change horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 < ‖p.2‖ at hp
      rw [horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass this] at hp
      rw [← norm_pos_iff]
      linarith

/-- **The event horizon is the hypersurface `‖x‖ = r_H(τ)` of the generator**: inside the ball
the outgoing light rays `r = 3(r_b(τ) − (τ_c − τ))` from the centre at `τ_c − 9M/2`, which cross
the boundary of the ball at `r = 2M` at `τ_H = τ_c − 4M/3`, and the sphere `r = 2M` after. -/
theorem eventHorizon_eq :
    eventHorizon M τc χb = {p : ℝ × E3 | ‖p.2‖ = horizonRadius M τc χb p.1} := by
  have hc : Continuous fun p : ℝ × E3 => horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 :=
    (continuous_horizonRadius hM hτc hχ hmass).comp continuous_fst
  have hn : Continuous fun p : ℝ × E3 => ‖p.2‖ := continuous_norm.comp continuous_snd
  rw [eventHorizon, causalPastScri_eq hM hτc hχ hmass]
  apply Subset.antisymm
  · intro p hp
    exact (frontier_lt_subset_eq hc hn hp).symm
  · intro p hp
    change ‖p.2‖ = horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 at hp
    rw [(isOpen_lt hc hn).frontier_eq]
    refine ⟨?_, fun h => by
      have h' : horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 < ‖p.2‖ := h
      rw [hp] at h'
      exact lt_irrefl _ h'⟩
    -- the points `(τ, x + t u)`, `t > 0`, lie above the generator
    set u := direction p.2
    have hu : ‖u‖ = 1 := norm_direction p.2
    have hxu : ‖p.2‖ • u = p.2 := norm_smul_direction p.2
    have ht : Tendsto (fun t : ℝ => (p.1, p.2 + t • u)) (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 p) := by
      have : Tendsto (fun t : ℝ => (p.1, p.2 + t • u)) (𝓝 0) (𝓝 (p.1, p.2 + (0 : ℝ) • u)) :=
        (continuous_const.prodMk (continuous_const.add (continuous_id.smul continuous_const)))
          |>.tendsto 0
      simpa using this.mono_left nhdsWithin_le_nhds
    refine mem_closure_of_tendsto ht ?_
    filter_upwards [self_mem_nhdsWithin] with t ht0
    change horizonRadius M τc χb p.1 < ‖p.2 + t • u‖
    rw [← hxu, ← add_smul, norm_smul, hu, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs,
      abs_of_pos (by have := norm_nonneg p.2; have : (0 : ℝ) < t := ht0; linarith)]
    have : (0 : ℝ) < t := ht0
    linarith

/-- **The generator is an outgoing radial null curve through the crossing of the stellar
surface with `r = 2M`**: for every unit vector `u`, wherever `r_H(τ) ≥ 0` the velocity
`(1, (1 − V) u)` of the curve `τ ↦ r_H(τ) u` (`hasDerivWithinAt_horizonRadius`) is null; the
generator meets the boundary of the ball at `r = 2M` at `τ_H = τ_c − 4M/3`, lies inside the ball
before (`horizonRadius_le_boundaryRadius`) and starts at the centre at `τ_c − 9M/2`. -/
theorem horizon_generator {u : E3} (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) :
    (∀ τ, 0 ≤ horizonRadius M τc χb τ →
      osForm M τc χb (τ, horizonRadius M τc χb τ • u)
        (1, (1 - infallSpeed M τc χb τ (horizonRadius M τc χb τ)) • u)
        (1, (1 - infallSpeed M τc χb τ (horizonRadius M τc χb τ)) • u) = 0) ∧
      horizonRadius M τc χb (τc - 4 * M / 3) = 2 * M ∧
      boundaryRadius τc χb (τc - 4 * M / 3) = 2 * M ∧
      horizonRadius M τc χb (τc - 9 * M / 2) = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun τ hτ => ?_, horizonRadius_of_le hM hτc hχ hmass le_rfl,
    boundaryRadius_horizonTime hM hτc hχ hmass, ?_⟩
  · rw [osForm_self, shift_smul hτ hu, ← add_smul, sub_add_cancel, one_smul, hu]
    norm_num
  · have hτ : τc - 9 * M / 2 ≤ τc - 4 * M / 3 := by linarith
    have hτ' : τc - 9 * M / 2 < τc := by linarith
    have hrb : boundaryRadius τc χb (τc - 9 * M / 2) = 9 * M / 2 := by
      refine (pow_left_inj₀ (boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ hτ').le (by positivity)
        three_ne_zero).mp ?_
      rw [boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass hτ']
      ring
    simp [horizonRadius, hτ, hrb]

/-- After `τ_H` the horizon is the sphere `r = 2M`, generated by the null curves `x = 2M u` of
constant radius: they are future causal curves that start on the generator and never escape
(`norm_le_horizonRadius` applies to them). -/
theorem isFutureCausalCurve_horizon {u : E3} (hu : ‖u‖ = 1) :
    IsFutureCausalCurve M τc χb (τc - 4 * M / 3) (fun _ => (2 * M) • u) := by
  have hnorm : ‖(2 * M) • u‖ = 2 * M := by
    rw [norm_smul, hu, mul_one, Real.norm_eq_abs, abs_of_pos (by positivity)]
  refine ⟨fun τ _ => Or.inr ?_, continuousOn_const, fun τ hτ => ⟨0,
    (hasDerivWithinAt_const τ _ _), ?_⟩⟩
  · rw [← norm_pos_iff, hnorm]
    positivity
  · rw [isFutureCausal_iff, zero_add, shift_smul (by positivity) hu,
      infallSpeed_two_mul hM hτc hχ hmass hτ, one_smul, hu]

end Horizon


/-! ### The chart of Painlevé and Gullstrand is the Oppenheimer–Snyder spacetime -/

section Charts

/-- The radial unit vector `(sin θ cos φ, sin θ sin φ, cos θ)`. -/
def sphDir (θ φ : ℝ) : E3 :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 ![Real.sin θ * Real.cos φ, Real.sin θ * Real.sin φ, Real.cos θ]

/-- `∂ω/∂θ`. -/
def sphDirθ (θ φ : ℝ) : E3 :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 ![Real.cos θ * Real.cos φ, Real.cos θ * Real.sin φ, -Real.sin θ]

/-- `∂ω/∂φ`. -/
def sphDirφ (θ φ : ℝ) : E3 :=
  WithLp.toLp 2 ![-(Real.sin θ * Real.sin φ), Real.sin θ * Real.cos φ, 0]

theorem inner_sphDir (θ φ : ℝ) :
    ⟪sphDir θ φ, sphDir θ φ⟫_ℝ = 1 ∧ ⟪sphDir θ φ, sphDirθ θ φ⟫_ℝ = 0 ∧
      ⟪sphDir θ φ, sphDirφ θ φ⟫_ℝ = 0 ∧ ⟪sphDirθ θ φ, sphDirθ θ φ⟫_ℝ = 1 ∧
      ⟪sphDirθ θ φ, sphDirφ θ φ⟫_ℝ = 0 ∧
      ⟪sphDirφ θ φ, sphDirφ θ φ⟫_ℝ = Real.sin θ ^ 2 := by
  have h1 := Real.sin_sq_add_cos_sq θ
  have h2 := Real.sin_sq_add_cos_sq φ
  simp only [sphDir, sphDirθ, sphDirφ, EuclideanSpace.inner_toLp_toLp, dotProduct,
    Fin.sum_univ_three, star_trivial]
  simp
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · linear_combination Real.sin θ ^ 2 * h2 + h1
  · linear_combination Real.sin θ * Real.cos θ * h2
  · ring
  · linear_combination Real.cos θ ^ 2 * h2 + h1
  · ring
  · linear_combination Real.sin θ ^ 2 * h2

theorem norm_sphDir (θ φ : ℝ) : ‖sphDir θ φ‖ = 1 := by
  have h := (inner_sphDir θ φ).1
  rw [real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq] at h
  have := norm_nonneg (sphDir θ φ)
  nlinarith

/-- The radial unit vector depends smoothly on the angles. -/
theorem hasFDerivAt_sphDir (x : E) :
    HasFDerivAt (fun y : E => sphDir (y 2) (y 3))
      ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj 2 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirθ (x 2) (x 3)) +
        (ContinuousLinearMap.proj 3 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirφ (x 2) (x 3))) x := by
  set e := (EuclideanSpace.equiv (Fin 3) ℝ).symm
  have hs2 := SchwarzschildExterior.hasFDerivAt_coord 2 (Real.hasDerivAt_sin (x 2))
  have hc2 := SchwarzschildExterior.hasFDerivAt_coord 2 (Real.hasDerivAt_cos (x 2))
  have hs3 := SchwarzschildExterior.hasFDerivAt_coord 3 (Real.hasDerivAt_sin (x 3))
  have hc3 := SchwarzschildExterior.hasFDerivAt_coord 3 (Real.hasDerivAt_cos (x 3))
  have hg : HasFDerivAt (fun y : E => (![Real.sin (y 2) * Real.cos (y 3),
      Real.sin (y 2) * Real.sin (y 3), Real.cos (y 2)] : Fin 3 → ℝ))
      (e.symm.toContinuousLinearMap.comp
        ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj 2 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirθ (x 2) (x 3)) +
          (ContinuousLinearMap.proj 3 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirφ (x 2) (x 3)))) x := by
    refine hasFDerivAt_pi'' fun i => ?_
    fin_cases i
    · refine (hs2.fun_mul hc3).congr_fderiv ?_
      ext v
      simp [e, sphDirθ, sphDirφ]
      ring
    · refine (hs2.fun_mul hs3).congr_fderiv ?_
      ext v
      simp [e, sphDirθ, sphDirφ]
      ring
    · refine hc2.congr_fderiv ?_
      ext v
      simp [e, sphDirθ, sphDirφ]
      ring
  have h := e.hasFDerivAt.comp x hg
  convert h using 1
  · funext y
    simp [e, sphDir]
  · ext v
    simp [e]

/-- The spherical chart `(τ, ρ, θ, φ) ↦ (τ, ρ(x) ω(θ, φ))` of a radius `ρ`. -/
def sphChart (ρ : E → ℝ) (x : E) : ℝ × E3 := (x 0, ρ x • sphDir (x 2) (x 3))

theorem hasFDerivAt_sphChart {ρ : E → ℝ} {ρ' : E →L[ℝ] ℝ} {x : E} (hρ : HasFDerivAt ρ ρ' x) :
    HasFDerivAt (sphChart ρ) ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj 0 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).prod
      (ρ x • ((ContinuousLinearMap.proj 2 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirθ (x 2) (x 3)) +
        (ContinuousLinearMap.proj 3 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ).smulRight (sphDirφ (x 2) (x 3))) +
        ρ'.smulRight (sphDir (x 2) (x 3)))) x :=
  (hasFDerivAt_apply 0 x).prodMk (hρ.smul (hasFDerivAt_sphDir x))

/-- **The metric in a spherical chart**: with `V = V(τ, ρ)`,
`g(Dv, Dw) = −v⁰w⁰ + (dρ(v) + V v⁰)(dρ(w) + V w⁰) + ρ²(v²w² + sin²θ v³w³)`. -/
theorem osForm_sphChart {ρ : E → ℝ} {ρ' : E →L[ℝ] ℝ} {x : E} (hρ : HasFDerivAt ρ ρ' x)
    (hρ0 : 0 ≤ ρ x) (v w : E) :
    osForm M τc χb (sphChart ρ x) (fderiv ℝ (sphChart ρ) x v) (fderiv ℝ (sphChart ρ) x w) =
      -(v 0 * w 0) + (ρ' v + infallSpeed M τc χb (x 0) (ρ x) * v 0) *
        (ρ' w + infallSpeed M τc χb (x 0) (ρ x) * w 0) +
        ρ x ^ 2 * (v 2 * w 2 + Real.sin (x 2) ^ 2 * (v 3 * w 3)) := by
  obtain ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6⟩ := inner_sphDir (x 2) (x 3)
  have h2' : ⟪sphDirθ (x 2) (x 3), sphDir (x 2) (x 3)⟫_ℝ = 0 := by rw [real_inner_comm]; exact h2
  have h3' : ⟪sphDirφ (x 2) (x 3), sphDir (x 2) (x 3)⟫_ℝ = 0 := by rw [real_inner_comm]; exact h3
  have h5' : ⟪sphDirφ (x 2) (x 3), sphDirθ (x 2) (x 3)⟫_ℝ = 0 := by rw [real_inner_comm]; exact h5
  rw [(hasFDerivAt_sphChart hρ).fderiv]
  simp only [osForm, sphChart, ContinuousLinearMap.prod_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.proj_apply,
    add_apply, smul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.smulRight_apply]
  rw [shift_smul hρ0 (norm_sphDir _ _)]
  simp only [inner_add_left, inner_add_right, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right, h1, h2, h3,
    h4, h5, h6, h2', h3', h5']
  simp
  ring


/-- **Inside the ball the metric is the flat dust ball**: the spherical chart
`(τ, χ, θ, φ) ↦ (τ, a(τ)χ ω(θ, φ))` pulls `osForm` back to the metric of `dustInterior`, for
`χ ≤ χ_b`. -/
theorem form_dust (hτc : 0 < τc) {x : E} (hx : x ∈ dustDomain τc) (hxb : x 1 ≤ χb) (v w : E) :
    osForm M τc χb (sphChart (fun y => dustScale τc (y 0) * y 1) x)
        (fderiv ℝ (sphChart (fun y => dustScale τc (y 0) * y 1)) x v)
        (fderiv ℝ (sphChart (fun y => dustScale τc (y 0) * y 1)) x w) =
      (dustInterior hτc).metric.form x v w := by
  have ha := dustScale_pos hτc hx.1
  have hs : 0 < τc - x 0 := sub_pos.mpr hx.1
  have hρ : HasFDerivAt (fun y : E => dustScale τc (y 0) * y 1)
      (dustScale τc (x 0) • (ContinuousLinearMap.proj 1 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ) +
        x 1 • ((-(2 / 3) * dustScale τc (x 0) / (τc - x 0)) •
          (ContinuousLinearMap.proj 0 : E →L[ℝ] ℝ))) x :=
    (SchwarzschildExterior.hasFDerivAt_coord 0 (hasDerivAt_dustScale hτc hx.1)).fun_mul
      (hasFDerivAt_apply 1 x)
  rw [osForm_sphChart hρ (mul_pos ha hx.2.1).le, ComovingData.metric_form_apply]
  have hV : infallSpeed M τc χb (x 0) (dustScale τc (x 0) * x 1) =
      2 / 3 * (dustScale τc (x 0) * x 1) / (τc - x 0) := by
    have hle : dustScale τc (x 0) * x 1 ≤ boundaryRadius τc χb (x 0) :=
      mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hxb ha.le
    simp [infallSpeed, hx.1, hle]
  rw [hV]
  simp only [add_apply, smul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.proj_apply, smul_eq_mul, dustInterior]
  field_simp
  ring

/-- **Outside the ball the metric is the Schwarzschild field**: the spherical chart
`(τ, R, θ, φ) ↦ (τ, r(τ, R) ω(θ, φ))` pulls `osForm` back to the Lemaître chart `lemaitre`, on the
shells `R ≥ τ_c` outside the ball. -/
theorem form_lemaitre (hM : 0 < M) (hτc : 0 < τc) (hχ : 0 < χb)
    (hmass : 9 * M * τc ^ 2 = 2 * χb ^ 3) {x : E} (hx : x ∈ lemaitreDomain) (hR : τc ≤ x 1)
    (v w : E) :
    osForm M τc χb (sphChart (lemaitreRadius M) x) (fderiv ℝ (sphChart (lemaitreRadius M)) x v)
        (fderiv ℝ (sphChart (lemaitreRadius M)) x w) = (lemaitre hM).metric.form x v w := by
  have hr := lemaitreRadius_pos hM hx.1
  have hd := sub_pos.mpr hx.1
  rw [osForm_sphChart (hasFDerivAt_lemaitreRadius hM hx.1) hr.le,
    ComovingData.metric_form_apply]
  have hout : τc ≤ x 0 ∨ boundaryRadius τc χb (x 0) ≤ lemaitreRadius M x := by
    rcases le_or_gt τc (x 0) with h | h
    · exact Or.inl h
    · right
      have hs : 0 < τc - x 0 := sub_pos.mpr h
      rw [le_iff_cube_le (boundaryRadius_pos hτc hχ h).le hr.le,
        boundaryRadius_cube hτc hmass h, lemaitreRadius_cube hM hx.1]
      have : (τc - x 0) ^ 2 ≤ (x 1 - x 0) ^ 2 := by nlinarith
      nlinarith
  rw [infallSpeed_eq_sqrt hM hτc hχ hmass hout, sqrt_two_mul_div_lemaitreRadius hM hx.1]
  have h3 := lemaitreRadius_cube hM hx.1
  simp only [sub_apply, smul_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.proj_apply, smul_eq_mul, lemaitre]
  field_simp
  linear_combination (4 * v 1 * w 1) * h3

end Charts

/- The hypotheses of the sections hold: for `M = 2/9`, `τ_c = 1` and `χ_b = 1` the mass relation
`9 M τ_c² = 2 χ_b³` is satisfied. -/
example : (0 : ℝ) < 2 / 9 ∧ (0 : ℝ) < 1 ∧ (0 : ℝ) < 1 ∧
    9 * (2 / 9 : ℝ) * 1 ^ 2 = 2 * 1 ^ 3 := by norm_num

end ProjectAinos.GeneralRelativity.CollapseHorizon
